0.0578,"playId":"401862824257","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0567,"playId":"401862824263","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0516,"playId":"401862824266","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0505,"playId":"401862824272","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0425,"playId":"401862824270","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0545,"playId":"401862824274","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0586,"playId":"401862824277","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0598,"playId":"401862824280","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0598,"playId":"401862824284","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0532,"playId":"401862824288","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.046,"playId":"401862824294","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0492,"playId":"401862824299","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0508,"playId":"401862824302","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0577,"playId":"401862824306","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0647,"playId":"401862824311","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0667,"playId":"401862824316","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1119,"playId":"401862824320","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1015,"playId":"401862824325","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0965,"playId":"401862824329","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.0724,"playId":"401862824333","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1231,"playId":"401862824339","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.1263,"playId":"401862824347","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3886","guid":"aab423e5-c4ef-3dd1-a6fb-cf7efdbe0be8","fullName":"Raymond James Stadium","address":{"city":"Tampa","state":"FL","zipCode":"33607","country":"USA"},"grass":true,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3886.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":0},"article":{"headline":"Stokes has 5 total TDs, Memphis blows 21-point lead before beating South Florida 52-41","description":"— Marcus Stokes threw three touchdown passes and added two rushing TDs and Memphis blew a 21-point lead before the Tigers beat South Florida 52-41 on Thursday night.","story":"TAMPA, Fla. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5165807/marcus-stokes\" target=\"_new\">Marcus Stokes</a> threw three touchdown passes and added two rushing TDs and Memphis blew a 21-point lead before the Tigers beat South Florida 52-41 on Thursday night. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5222671/jaylin-carter\" target=\"_new\">Jaylin Carter</a> had 109 yards rushing and two touchdowns on 21 carries for Memphis (8-2, 5-1 American Conference). \n\n\r\n              The Tigers, who won <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/memphis-charlotte-score-6032cea287af503d35edd8e6f1f8d546\">59-8</a> at Charlotte on Oct. 3, are the only team in the Bowl Subdivision with 50-plus points in multiple road games this season. \n\n\r\n              Stokes was 15-of-31 passing for 313 yards with no interceptions and finished with 73 yards rushing on eight carries. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079542/luke-kromenhoek\" target=\"_new\">Luke Kromenhoek</a>, who made his fourth career start, had 271 yards passing and three touchdowns to go with a 146 yards rushing and a score on 30 carries or South Florida (6-4, 2-4). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5154559/jason-collins-jr\" target=\"_new\">Jason Collins Jr</a>. had a 13-yard touchdown reception and added a 75-yard rushing TD. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5149075/nico-gramatica\" target=\"_new\">Nico Gramatica</a>, who made a 47-yard field goal in the second quarter, kicked a 38-yarder with 8:04 to play that gave South Florida its first lead at 41-38.\n\n\r\n              Two plays from scrimmage later, Stokes hit <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5294438/jemyri-davis\" target=\"_new\">Jemyri Davis</a> for a 76-yard touchdown.\n\n\r\n              The Bulls marched deep into Memphis territory before Kromenhoek’s pass on fourth-and-2 was dropped in the end zone by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870927/bryson-rodgers\" target=\"_new\">Bryson Rodgers</a> with 3:38 to play.\n\n\r\n              After the Tigers went three-and-out, Harrison Tuck’s 51-yard punt from the back of the end zone gave USF possession at its 47. Collins was stopped for a 5-yard loss before J’Mond Tapp had back-to-back sacks before an incomplete pass on fourth-and-27 with 57 seconds left. \n\n\r\n              Carter capped the scoring with a 26-yard rushing TD. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next </hl2>\r\n              Memphis: Visits Navy on Nov. 21. \n\n\r\n              South Florida: Plays Nov. 21 at Florida Atlantic. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-13T05:13:33Z"}}